<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<SActionScript version="1" name="plugin_native_editor">

  <!-- Proposal 33 M6, the APP half — and the first gate this feature has ever
       had above the engine ABI.

       WHAT MAKES IT POSSIBLE. Everything in proposal 33 above twPluginEditor
       was ungated because a plugin GUI needs a window, and a qxa run uses the
       REAL platform plugin (the suite does not set QT_QPA_PLATFORM=offscreen),
       so a case that opened one would put a dialog on the developer's desktop
       in the middle of the suite. `tw.test.clap.gui` removes the window from
       the question: it implements clap.gui and CREATES NOTHING — create() and
       set_parent() succeed and allocate no window at all — so the whole
       PARAMETER FLOW can be driven with no display, which is the part of M6
       that can actually be wrong. The verb opens the editor with
       showWindow = false; the attach, the container's native handle, the 30 Hz
       poll timer and every action it submits are the production ones.

       The fixture stands in for a user turning a knob: its gui->show() sets
       Gain to 2.5 INTERNALLY (as a real plugin does — its DSP follows its own
       GUI without asking the host) and then calls
       clap_host_params->request_flush, which is the only route a CLAP edit has
       out of the plugin while nothing is rendering.

       What is being gated:

       1. THE FALLBACK DECISION. A CLAP plugin WITH a native editor must now
          resolve to "native" — proposal 33 D3's "the slider list is not
          reachable alongside a native GUI" is only safe if that decision is
          right. plugin_ui_strip_and_editor asserts the other two answers
          ("generic" for a CLAP with no GUI, "none" for a Missing slot); this
          is the third.

       2. THE EDIT IS AUDIBLE. The knob the plugin turned reaches the DSP and
          the render. Gain 2.5 on tw.test.clap.gui (out = in * gain) takes the
          first second of ../test_sawtooth.wav from 0.0667 to 0.1666 - measured,
          and exactly 2.5x. Nothing in the script sets that parameter: the
          plugin did.

       3. THE EDIT IS ONE UNDO ENTRY, and undoing it puts the level back. This
          is proposal 33 M5's central claim, it had no gate at all, AND IT WAS
          BROKEN: SSetPluginParamAction::apply() built its inverse from
          getParam(), but a native-editor edit has already reached the plugin by
          the time the app hears about it (poll() writes the mirror and the DSP
          on its way through, which is what makes a knob audible whatever the
          host does). The baseline was therefore the NEW value, the inverse
          restored what it had just set, and undo was a silent no-op. Watched
          failing here before the fix: this render read 0.1666 - the gained
          level - where it now reads 0.0667. The pre-edit value now travels
          with the edit (twEditorParamEdit::previousValue).

       4. The window closes, and the plugin is not torn down with an editor
          still open (which the backend reports as an error). -->

  <setup project="new"/>

  <actions>
    <add-track index="-1"/>
    <add-sample trackIndex="0" filePath="../test_sawtooth.wav" timePos="0"/>

    <insert-plugin trackPath="0" slotIndex="0"
                   format="clap" uid="tw.test.clap.gui"
                   name="Smaragd Test GUI" vendor="Smaragd"
                   path="twtestclap.clap" nIn="2" nOut="2"/>

    <!-- 1. The fallback decision, now that a CLAP can answer "native". -->
    <assert-plugin-editor-kind trackIndex="0" slotIndex="0" expect="native"/>

    <!-- The unity baseline, before any window exists. -->
    <render filename="pne_base.wav" format="wav" quality="10" durationSec="1.5"/>
    <assert-audio-energy filename="pne_base.wav"
                         startFrame="0" frameCount="48000"
                         channel="0" minRms="0.060" maxRms="0.074"/>

    <!-- 2. Open the plugin's own interface. The fixture turns its Gain knob to
         2.5 on show() and asks the host to flush; the 30 Hz poll is what
         collects it, so the wait is doing real work, not padding. -->
    <plugin-native-editor trackIndex="0" slotIndex="0" action="open" expectOpen="1"/>
    <wait-ms ms="250"/>

    <render filename="pne_gui_gain.wav" format="wav" quality="10" durationSec="1.5"/>
    <assert-audio-energy filename="pne_gui_gain.wav"
                         startFrame="0" frameCount="48000"
                         channel="0" minRms="0.155" maxRms="0.180"/>

    <!-- 3. ONE undo entry for the gesture, and it restores the level. -->
    <undo count="1"/>

    <render filename="pne_undone.wav" format="wav" quality="10" durationSec="1.5"/>
    <assert-audio-energy filename="pne_undone.wav"
                         startFrame="0" frameCount="48000"
                         channel="0" minRms="0.060" maxRms="0.074"/>

    <!-- 4. Take the window down. An editor alive when its plugin is destroyed
         is a contract violation the CLAP backend logs as an error. -->
    <plugin-native-editor trackIndex="0" slotIndex="0" action="close" expectOpen="0"/>
  </actions>

  <assertions>
    <assert-track-count equals="1"/>
  </assertions>

</SActionScript>
